# i18n — agents never edit CSV

Do **not** modify `BelzontTLM/i18n/i18n.csv`, `i18n.xlsm`, or locale CSVs. Humans merge via Excel macros.

## New short strings

Create or append a tab-separated file:

`BelzontTLM/i18n/{feature}_entries.txt`

(same naming as existing `sipManagedGroups_entries.txt`, etc.)

### Format (7 columns, tab-separated)

```text
K45::XTM	vuio	lineStationDetail	waiting.passengers	K45::XTM.vuio[lineStationDetail.waiting.passengers]	Passengers waiting: {quantity}	Passageiros aguardando: {quantity}
::T	UI			::TUI	UI	UI
```

| Col | Meaning |
|---|---|
| 1 | prefix (`K45::XTM` or `::T` / `::G` / …) |
| 2 | module (`vuio`) or empty for `::` rows |
| 3 | group / namespace |
| 4 | key segment |
| 5 | assembled key (what code / CSV will use) |
| 6 | en-US |
| 7 | pt-BR |

Older in-repo `*_entries.txt` files may have 6 columns (no assembled key). **New agent output uses 7 columns.**

## Long-form / markdown bodies

For glossary section bodies and other multiline markdown, do **not** use `*_entries.txt`. Create one file per locale under:

`BelzontTLM/i18n/{langCode}/{key}.md`

Example: `BelzontTLM/i18n/en-US/` and `BelzontTLM/i18n/pt-BR/`.

```markdown
---
key: K45::XTM.vuio[glossary.section.smoke]
---
Long **markdown** body for this locale.
```

- Frontmatter field **`key`** (alias **`entry`**) = assembled locale id.
- Body after frontmatter = locale value (newlines preserved).
- Filename should match the key when the filesystem allows; frontmatter is authoritative.
- **`en-US/` is the base:** every language gets those entries first. If a key/file is missing under another `i18n/{lang}/`, the en-US body is used. Present lang files overlay en-US for matching keys.
- Loaded by `BasicIMod.LoadLocales` after CSV; **last loaded wins** on key conflict (lang md overlays en-US md; md overrides CSV for the same key).
- Still never edit `i18n.csv`.
- Always add entries to all other languages csv files when adding new en-EN entries.
- Glossary bodies are shown with **`MarkdownRenderer`** — use the **Markdown** dialect below.
- Encyclopedia/glossary **images and links belong in the i18n md body** (`![alt](src)`, `[label](data)`), not as separate non-md content for the section. See `.klyte-kanban/RefsLibrary/vanilla-glossary.md`.
- Glossary images use the same sizing as vanilla tutorial/glossary content: default height **300rem**, max width **850rem**, centered. Optional per-image height override (vanilla `height:` suffix) goes in the markdown `src`:

```markdown
![Screenshot of the line listing](coui://xtm.k45/UI/images/xtm-overview-modes.jpg)
![Taller screenshot](coui://xtm.k45/UI/images/xtm-overview-modes.jpg height:420)
```

  Prefer `coui://xtm.k45/UI/images/...` for mod-shipped encyclopedia screenshots. Do not rely on CSS `height: auto` — Gameface collapses that to 0.

## FormattedParagraphs / formatted text

Formatting codes are **game-ui renderer dialects**, not Managed C#. `FormattedParagraphs` splits on newlines; each paragraph is rendered by `FormattedText` with either:

- **Markup** (default `MarkupRenderer`) — short strings in default `FormattedParagraphs` (e.g. SIP / managed groups)
- **Markdown** (`new MarkdownRenderer()` / glossary) — long-form `i18n/{lang}/*.md` bodies

Pick the dialect by where the string is shown. Do **not** invent HTML, CSS, or markdown beyond the chosen dialect.

| Feature | Markup (default) | Markdown (glossary / opt-in) |
|---|---|---|
| Bold | `**text**` | `**text**` |
| Escape `*` | `\*` | (not supported) |
| List item | paragraph starts with `- ` | (not supported) |
| Headings | (not supported) | leading `#` … `###### ` |
| Line break in paragraph | (not supported) | `<br>` (any case) |
| Links | `<data>` or `<data\|label>` | `[label](data)` |
| Images | (not supported) | `![alt](src)` or `![alt](src height:N)` |
| Newlines | separate paragraphs | separate paragraphs |

Also unsupported in both: single-`*` italics, tables, arbitrary HTML.

Tutorial link prefixes inside Markup `<…>` data (`inputAction:`, `icon:`, `image:`) only work when `tutorialTextRenderer` is wired — **do not use** them in general i18n unless that renderer is in place.

## `::` special keys

Resolved at load by `BasicIMod.ProcessKey`. Prefixes (see `BelzontCommons/README.md`):

`::M`, `::G{group}`, `::T{tab}`, `::L{prop}`, `::D{prop}`, `::B{action}`, `::H{action}`, `::E{Type}.{value}`, `::NT{id}`, `::ND{id}`

For `::` rows: leave unused middle columns empty; column 5 is the CSV key (e.g. `::TUI`). Do not invent new `::` shapes — consult `BasicIMod` / Commons README when unsure.

Frontend/C# should reference the **assembled** key; agents only write the pending `*_entries.txt` or `i18n/{lang}/*.md`.

## `translate` fallbacks

Do **not** pass a fallback to `translate` / `engine.translate` for **new** entries unless the user **explicitly** asks for one.

```ts
// ❌ BAD (new code)
translate("lineStationDetail.waiting.passengers", "Passengers waiting")

// ✅ GOOD
translate("lineStationDetail.waiting.passengers")
```

When editing a file for any other reason, **remove fallbacks** from existing `translate(...)` / `engine.translate(...)` calls in the code you touch (opportunistic cleanup). Do not do a repo-wide sweep unless asked.
